      ":question/id": "0a04f2ba-f758-511c-bedb-1ff1640b14ae",
      ":question/problem": "Find $q$, if $5{a}_{1}+q{a}_{2}=b$ and\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}-9 \\\\ -16 \\\\ -13 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate the $q$ term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{a}_{1}+q{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ 5\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}+q\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-9 \\\\ -16 \\\\ -13 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ q\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-9 \\\\ -16 \\\\ -13 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}-5\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ q\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the final equation above, we can tell that $q=-2.$",
